139→
140→## Section 3: HashToPoint — Poseidon XOF with Base-Q Extraction
141→
142→### Architecture
143→
144→1. Poseidon sponge (rate=2, capacity=1) in XOF mode
145→2. Absorb: message + salt
146→3. Squeeze: permute, extract 12 Zq coefficients from each of s0 and s1 (24 per permutation)
147→4. Extraction: felt252 → u256 → (low u128, high u128) → 6 DivRem-by-Q per half → 12 Zq per felt252
148→
149→### Why Base-Q Instead of b-bit Limbs
150→
151→| | b-bit limb → mod Q | Base-Q DivRem |
152→|---|---|---|
153→| Coeffs/felt252 | 4 (b=64) | **12** |
154→| Squeeze perms | 64 | **22** (2.9x fewer) |
155→| Extra mod Q step | Yes | **No** (RemT = Zq) |
156→
157→Same security: each coefficient comes from reducing a ≥50-bit value mod Q (per Renyi analysis, ≤0.37 bits loss at b=50).
158→
159→### Renyi Safety Analysis
160→
161→From u128 (128 bits), repeated DivRem by Q ≈ 13.585 bits per coefficient:
162→
163→| Coeff | Input bits | Safe (≥50)? |
164→|-------|-----------|-------------|
165→| 1 | 128.0 | yes |
166→| 2 | 114.4 | yes |
167→| 3 | 100.8 | yes |
168→| 4 | 87.2 | yes |
169→| 5 | 73.6 | yes |
170→| 6 | 60.0 | yes |
171→| 7 | 46.5 | **no** (discard) |
172→
173→6 safe coefficients per u128 half → 12 per felt252 → 24 per squeeze permutation.
174→
175→### Two Separate DivRem Chains
176→
177→The high u128 from `u128s_from_felt252` is bounded by the Stark prime:
178→
179→```
180→P = 2^251 + 17 * 2^192 + 1
181→high_max = (P - 1) >> 128 = 10633823966279327296825105735305134080   (124 bits)
182→```
183→
184→This is tighter than u128 (128 bits), so we use two separate type chains with exact bounds.
185→
186→**LOW chain (u128, 128 bits → 6 Zq):**
187→
188→```cairo
189→// Starting type: u128
190→
191→type ExtractLQ1 = BoundedInt<0, 27689996494502275487295516920153650>;     // 115 bits
192→type ExtractLQ2 = BoundedInt<0, 2253234314793903123711898195146>;         // 101 bits
193→type ExtractLQ3 = BoundedInt<0, 183353756594833031468133956>;             // 88 bits
194→type ExtractLQ4 = BoundedInt<0, 14920152705251284194656>;                 // 74 bits
195→type ExtractLQ5 = BoundedInt<0, 1214106331292317047>;                     // 61 bits
196→type ExtractLQ6 = BoundedInt<0, 98796186125178>;                          // 47 bits (discarded)
197→
198→impl DivRemLQ0 of DivRemHelper<u128, QConst>       { type DivT = ExtractLQ1; type RemT = Zq; }
199→impl DivRemLQ1 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ1, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ2; type RemT = Zq; }
200→impl DivRemLQ2 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ2, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ3; type RemT = Zq; }
201→impl DivRemLQ3 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ3, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ4; type RemT = Zq; }
202→impl DivRemLQ4 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ4, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ5; type RemT = Zq; }
203→impl DivRemLQ5 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ5, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ6; type RemT = Zq; }
204→```
205→
206→**HIGH chain (FeltHigh, 124 bits → 6 Zq):**
207→
208→```cairo
209→type FeltHigh = BoundedInt<0, 10633823966279327296825105735305134080>;    // 124 bits
210→
211→type ExtractHQ1 = BoundedInt<0, 865312390453196134496306105891865>;       // 110 bits
212→type ExtractHQ2 = BoundedInt<0, 70413572337309474692514126933>;           // 96 bits
213→type ExtractHQ3 = BoundedInt<0, 5729804893588532402352846>;               // 83 bits
214→type ExtractHQ4 = BoundedInt<0, 466254772039102644833>;                   // 69 bits
215→type ExtractHQ5 = BoundedInt<0, 37940822852884908>;                       // 56 bits
216→type ExtractHQ6 = BoundedInt<0, 3087380816411>;                           // 42 bits (discarded)
217→
218→impl DivRemHQ0 of DivRemHelper<FeltHigh, QConst>    { type DivT = ExtractHQ1; type RemT = Zq; }
219→impl DivRemHQ1 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ1, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ2; type RemT = Zq; }
220→impl DivRemHQ2 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ2, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ3; type RemT = Zq; }
221→impl DivRemHQ3 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ3, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ4; type RemT = Zq; }
222→impl DivRemHQ4 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ4, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ5; type RemT = Zq; }
223→impl DivRemHQ5 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ5, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ6; type RemT = Zq; }
224→```
225→
226→One `downcast(high)` from u128 → FeltHigh per felt252 (44 total, negligible vs hades cost).
227→
228→**Type count:** 12 quotient types + 1 FeltHigh + 12 DivRemHelper impls = **25 definitions**.
229→
230→### XOF Construction
231→
232→```cairo
233→use core::poseidon::hades_permutation;
234→
235→fn hash_to_point(message: Span<felt252>, salt: Span<felt252>) -> Array<u16> {
236→    let (mut s0, mut s1, mut s2): (felt252, felt252, felt252) = (0, 0, 0);
237→
238→    // Absorb message then salt (rate=2: pairs per permutation)
239→    absorb(ref s0, ref s1, ref s2, message);
240→    absorb(ref s0, ref s1, ref s2, salt);
241→    s2 += 1;  // domain separation before squeeze
242→
243→    // Squeeze: permute → extract 12 coefficients from each of s0, s1
244→    let mut coeffs: Array<u16> = array![];
245→    loop {
246→        let (ns0, ns1, ns2) = hades_permutation(s0, s1, s2);
247→        s0 = ns0; s1 = ns1; s2 = ns2;
248→        extract_12_from_felt252(s0, ref coeffs);
249→        if coeffs.len() >= 512 { break; }
250→        extract_12_from_felt252(s1, ref coeffs);
251→        if coeffs.len() >= 512 { break; }
252→    };
253→    // Truncate to exactly 512 via slice
254→    ...
255→}
256→
257→fn absorb(ref s0: felt252, ref s1: felt252, ref s2: felt252, mut input: Span<felt252>) {
258→    loop {
259→        match input.pop_front() {
260→            Option::None => { break; },
261→            Option::Some(first) => {
262→                let second = match input.pop_front() {
263→                    Option::Some(v) => *v,
264→                    Option::None => 1,  // pad
265→                };
266→                let (ns0, ns1, ns2) = hades_permutation(s0 + *first, s1 + second, s2);
267→                s0 = ns0; s1 = ns1; s2 = ns2;
268→            }
269→        }
270→    };
271→}
272→```
273→
274→### Extraction
275→
276→```cairo
277→fn extract_12_from_felt252(value: felt252, ref coeffs: Array<u16>) {
278→    match u128s_from_felt252(value) {
279→        U128sFromFelt252Result::Narrow(low) => {
280→            extract_6_from_low(low, ref coeffs);
281→        },
282→        U128sFromFelt252Result::Wide((high, low)) => {
283→            extract_6_from_low(low, ref coeffs);
284→            let high_bounded: FeltHigh = downcast(high).unwrap();
285→            extract_6_from_high(high_bounded, ref coeffs);
286→        },
287→    }
288→}
289→
290→fn extract_6_from_low(value: u128, ref coeffs: Array<u16>) {
291→    let (q1, r0) = bounded_int_div_rem(value, nz_q_extract());
292→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r0));
293→
294→    let (q2, r1) = bounded_int_div_rem(q1, nz_q_extract());
295→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r1));
296→
297→    let (q3, r2) = bounded_int_div_rem(q2, nz_q_extract());
298→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r2));
299→
300→    let (q4, r3) = bounded_int_div_rem(q3, nz_q_extract());
301→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r3));
302→
303→    let (q5, r4) = bounded_int_div_rem(q4, nz_q_extract());
304→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r4));
305→
306→    let (_q6, r5) = bounded_int_div_rem(q5, nz_q_extract());
307→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r5));
308→}
309→// extract_6_from_high: identical structure, uses HIGH chain types
310→```
311→
312→### Permutation Budget
313→
314→- Absorption: ~2 permutations (typical 3-element input: tx hash + 2 salt)
315→- Squeeze: 22 permutations
316→- **Total: ~24 hades_permutation calls**
