 41→}
 42→```
 43→
 44→Inspired by garaga's `ECDSASignatureWithHint` pattern: signature bundled with computation hints.
 45→
 46→### HashToPoint Trait
 47→
 48→```cairo
 49→trait HashToPoint<H> {
 50→    fn hash_to_point(message: Span<felt252>, salt: Span<felt252>) -> Array<u16>;
 51→}
 52→```
 53→
 54→### Verify Function
 55→
 56→```cairo
 57→fn verify<H, +HashToPoint<H>, +Drop<H>>(
 58→    pk: @FalconPublicKey,
 59→    sig_with_hint: FalconSignatureWithHint,
 60→    message: Span<felt252>,
 61→) -> bool {
 62→    // 1. msg_point = H::hash_to_point(message, sig.salt.span())
 63→    // 2. s1_ntt = ntt_fast(sig.s1.span())              — 1st NTT
 64→    // 3. product_ntt = mul_ntt(s1_ntt, pk.h_ntt.span())
 65→    // 4. product = intt_with_hint(product_ntt, hint.mul_hint.span())  — 2nd NTT (verify hint)
 66→    // 5. s0 = sub_zq(msg_point, product)
 67→    // 6. norm_check(s0, s1) <= SIG_BOUND (34034726 for Falcon-512)
 68→}
 69→```
 70→
 71→**Cost:** 2 NTTs, 0 INTTs. Reuses existing `ntt_fast`, `mul_ntt`, `sub_zq`, `intt_with_hint` from `ntt.cairo`. Existing `verify_uncompressed` kept as reference.
 72→
 73→---
 74→
 75→## Section 2: Base-Q Packing Module
 76→
 77→### Design
 78→
 79→Pack 512 Zq values (each in [0, 12288]) as polynomials in base Q = 12289:
 80→
 81→```
 82→felt252 = v0 + v1*Q + v2*Q^2 + ... + v17*Q^17
 83→```
 84→
 85→DivRem by Q gives `RemT = Zq` directly — **zero downcasts** needed.
 86→
 87→### Layout
 88→
 89→- 9 values per u128 half (Q^9 ≈ 2^122.3 < 2^128)
 90→- 18 values per felt252 (low u128 + high u128)
 91→- **29 storage slots** for 512 values (28 full + 1 partial with 8 values)
 92→
 93→### Accumulator Type Chain
 94→
 95→Shared between Horner packing and DivRem unpacking. AccN max = Q^(N+1) - 1:
 96→
 97→```
 98→Acc0 = Zq                          = BoundedInt<0, 12288>
 99→Acc1 = BoundedInt<0, 151019520>                              // Q^2 - 1
100→Acc2 = BoundedInt<0, 1855878893568>                          // Q^3 - 1
101→Acc3 = BoundedInt<0, 22806895723069440>                      // Q^4 - 1
102→Acc4 = BoundedInt<0, 280273941540800360448>                  // Q^5 - 1
103→Acc5 = BoundedInt<0, 3444286467594895629557760>              // Q^6 - 1
104→Acc6 = BoundedInt<0, 42326836400273672391635324928>          // Q^7 - 1
105→Acc7 = BoundedInt<0, 520154492522963160020806508052480>      // Q^8 - 1
106→Acc8 = BoundedInt<0, 6392178558614694273495691177456939008>  // Q^9 - 1
107→```
108→
109→### Packing (Horner)
110→
111→```cairo
112→// acc = v_i + Q * acc_prev
113→acc = add(v, mul(Q_CONST, acc_prev))
114→```
115→
116→Uses `MulHelper<QConst, AccN>` and `AddHelper<Zq, MulQAccN>` at each level.
117→
118→### Unpacking (DivRem chain)
119→
120→```cairo
121→let (acc_prev, v_i) = bounded_int_div_rem(acc, nz_q());
122→// acc_prev: AccN-1, v_i: Zq
123→```
124→
125→Uses `DivRemHelper<AccN, QConst>` → `(DivT = AccN-1, RemT = Zq)`.
126→
127→### Type Count
128→
129→40 definitions total per u128 half:
130→- 8 AccN types (Acc1–Acc8, Acc0 = Zq reused)
131→- 8 MulQAccN intermediate types
132→- 8 MulHelper impls
133→- 8 AddHelper impls
134→- 8 DivRemHelper impls
135→
136→`QConst`, `nz_q()`, `Zq` all reused from existing `zq.cairo`.
137→
138→---
139→
140→## Section 3: HashToPoint — Poseidon XOF with Base-Q Extraction
141→
142→### Architecture
143→
144→1. Poseidon sponge (rate=2, capacity=1) in XOF mode
145→2. Absorb: message + salt
146→3. Squeeze: permute, extract 12 Zq coefficients from each of s0 and s1 (24 per permutation)
147→4. Extraction: felt252 → u256 → (low u128, high u128) → 6 DivRem-by-Q per half → 12 Zq per felt252
148→
149→### Why Base-Q Instead of b-bit Limbs
150→
151→| | b-bit limb → mod Q | Base-Q DivRem |
152→|---|---|---|
153→| Coeffs/felt252 | 4 (b=64) | **12** |
154→| Squeeze perms | 64 | **22** (2.9x fewer) |
155→| Extra mod Q step | Yes | **No** (RemT = Zq) |
156→
157→Same security: each coefficient comes from reducing a ≥50-bit value mod Q (per Renyi analysis, ≤0.37 bits loss at b=50).
158→
159→### Renyi Safety Analysis
160→
161→From u128 (128 bits), repeated DivRem by Q ≈ 13.585 bits per coefficient:
162→
163→| Coeff | Input bits | Safe (≥50)? |
164→|-------|-----------|-------------|
165→| 1 | 128.0 | yes |
166→| 2 | 114.4 | yes |
167→| 3 | 100.8 | yes |
168→| 4 | 87.2 | yes |
169→| 5 | 73.6 | yes |
170→| 6 | 60.0 | yes |
171→| 7 | 46.5 | **no** (discard) |
172→
173→6 safe coefficients per u128 half → 12 per felt252 → 24 per squeeze permutation.
174→
175→### Two Separate DivRem Chains
176→
177→The high u128 from `u128s_from_felt252` is bounded by the Stark prime:
178→
179→```
180→P = 2^251 + 17 * 2^192 + 1
181→high_max = (P - 1) >> 128 = 10633823966279327296825105735305134080   (124 bits)
182→```
183→
184→This is tighter than u128 (128 bits), so we use two separate type chains with exact bounds.
185→
186→**LOW chain (u128, 128 bits → 6 Zq):**
187→
188→```cairo
189→// Starting type: u128
190→
191→type ExtractLQ1 = BoundedInt<0, 27689996494502275487295516920153650>;     // 115 bits
192→type ExtractLQ2 = BoundedInt<0, 2253234314793903123711898195146>;         // 101 bits
193→type ExtractLQ3 = BoundedInt<0, 183353756594833031468133956>;             // 88 bits
194→type ExtractLQ4 = BoundedInt<0, 14920152705251284194656>;                 // 74 bits
195→type ExtractLQ5 = BoundedInt<0, 1214106331292317047>;                     // 61 bits
196→type ExtractLQ6 = BoundedInt<0, 98796186125178>;                          // 47 bits (discarded)
197→
198→impl DivRemLQ0 of DivRemHelper<u128, QConst>       { type DivT = ExtractLQ1; type RemT = Zq; }
199→impl DivRemLQ1 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ1, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ2; type RemT = Zq; }
200→impl DivRemLQ2 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ2, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ3; type RemT = Zq; }
201→impl DivRemLQ3 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ3, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ4; type RemT = Zq; }
202→impl DivRemLQ4 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ4, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ5; type RemT = Zq; }
203→impl DivRemLQ5 of DivRemHelper<ExtractLQ5, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractLQ6; type RemT = Zq; }
204→```
205→
206→**HIGH chain (FeltHigh, 124 bits → 6 Zq):**
207→
208→```cairo
209→type FeltHigh = BoundedInt<0, 10633823966279327296825105735305134080>;    // 124 bits
210→
211→type ExtractHQ1 = BoundedInt<0, 865312390453196134496306105891865>;       // 110 bits
212→type ExtractHQ2 = BoundedInt<0, 70413572337309474692514126933>;           // 96 bits
213→type ExtractHQ3 = BoundedInt<0, 5729804893588532402352846>;               // 83 bits
214→type ExtractHQ4 = BoundedInt<0, 466254772039102644833>;                   // 69 bits
215→type ExtractHQ5 = BoundedInt<0, 37940822852884908>;                       // 56 bits
216→type ExtractHQ6 = BoundedInt<0, 3087380816411>;                           // 42 bits (discarded)
217→
218→impl DivRemHQ0 of DivRemHelper<FeltHigh, QConst>    { type DivT = ExtractHQ1; type RemT = Zq; }
219→impl DivRemHQ1 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ1, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ2; type RemT = Zq; }
220→impl DivRemHQ2 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ2, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ3; type RemT = Zq; }
221→impl DivRemHQ3 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ3, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ4; type RemT = Zq; }
222→impl DivRemHQ4 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ4, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ5; type RemT = Zq; }
223→impl DivRemHQ5 of DivRemHelper<ExtractHQ5, QConst>  { type DivT = ExtractHQ6; type RemT = Zq; }
224→```
225→
226→One `downcast(high)` from u128 → FeltHigh per felt252 (44 total, negligible vs hades cost).
227→
228→**Type count:** 12 quotient types + 1 FeltHigh + 12 DivRemHelper impls = **25 definitions**.
229→
230→### XOF Construction
231→
232→```cairo
233→use core::poseidon::hades_permutation;
234→
235→fn hash_to_point(message: Span<felt252>, salt: Span<felt252>) -> Array<u16> {
236→    let (mut s0, mut s1, mut s2): (felt252, felt252, felt252) = (0, 0, 0);
237→
238→    // Absorb message then salt (rate=2: pairs per permutation)
239→    absorb(ref s0, ref s1, ref s2, message);
240→    absorb(ref s0, ref s1, ref s2, salt);
241→    s2 += 1;  // domain separation before squeeze
242→
243→    // Squeeze: permute → extract 12 coefficients from each of s0, s1
244→    let mut coeffs: Array<u16> = array![];
245→    loop {
246→        let (ns0, ns1, ns2) = hades_permutation(s0, s1, s2);
247→        s0 = ns0; s1 = ns1; s2 = ns2;
248→        extract_12_from_felt252(s0, ref coeffs);
249→        if coeffs.len() >= 512 { break; }
250→        extract_12_from_felt252(s1, ref coeffs);
251→        if coeffs.len() >= 512 { break; }
252→    };
253→    // Truncate to exactly 512 via slice
254→    ...
255→}
256→
257→fn absorb(ref s0: felt252, ref s1: felt252, ref s2: felt252, mut input: Span<felt252>) {
258→    loop {
259→        match input.pop_front() {
260→            Option::None => { break; },
261→            Option::Some(first) => {
262→                let second = match input.pop_front() {
263→                    Option::Some(v) => *v,
264→                    Option::None => 1,  // pad
265→                };
266→                let (ns0, ns1, ns2) = hades_permutation(s0 + *first, s1 + second, s2);
267→                s0 = ns0; s1 = ns1; s2 = ns2;
268→            }
269→        }
270→    };
271→}
272→```
273→
274→### Extraction
275→
276→```cairo
277→fn extract_12_from_felt252(value: felt252, ref coeffs: Array<u16>) {
278→    match u128s_from_felt252(value) {
279→        U128sFromFelt252Result::Narrow(low) => {
280→            extract_6_from_low(low, ref coeffs);
281→        },
282→        U128sFromFelt252Result::Wide((high, low)) => {
283→            extract_6_from_low(low, ref coeffs);
284→            let high_bounded: FeltHigh = downcast(high).unwrap();
285→            extract_6_from_high(high_bounded, ref coeffs);
286→        },
287→    }
288→}
289→
290→fn extract_6_from_low(value: u128, ref coeffs: Array<u16>) {
291→    let (q1, r0) = bounded_int_div_rem(value, nz_q_extract());
292→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r0));
293→
294→    let (q2, r1) = bounded_int_div_rem(q1, nz_q_extract());
295→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r1));
296→
297→    let (q3, r2) = bounded_int_div_rem(q2, nz_q_extract());
298→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r2));
299→
300→    let (q4, r3) = bounded_int_div_rem(q3, nz_q_extract());
301→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r3));
302→
303→    let (q5, r4) = bounded_int_div_rem(q4, nz_q_extract());
304→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r4));
305→
306→    let (_q6, r5) = bounded_int_div_rem(q5, nz_q_extract());
307→    coeffs.append(upcast::<Zq, u16>(r5));
308→}
309→// extract_6_from_high: identical structure, uses HIGH chain types
310→```
311→
312→### Permutation Budget
313→
314→- Absorption: ~2 permutations (typical 3-element input: tx hash + 2 salt)
315→- Squeeze: 22 permutations
316→- **Total: ~24 hades_permutation calls**
317→
318→---
319→
320→## Section 4: Rust Tooling (falcon-rs)
321→
322→### Dependencies
323→
324→```toml
325→[dependencies]
326→lambdaworks-crypto = "0.13"
327→lambdaworks-math = "0.13"
328→serde = { version = "1", features = ["derive"] }
329→serde_json = "1"
330→```
331→
332→### Imports (matching garaga pattern)
333→
334→```rust
335→use lambdaworks_crypto::hash::poseidon::starknet::PoseidonCairoStark252;
336→use lambdaworks_crypto::hash::poseidon::Poseidon;
337→use lambdaworks_math::field::element::FieldElement;
338→use lambdaworks_math::field::fields::fft_friendly::stark_252_prime_field::Stark252PrimeField;
339→
340→type Felt = FieldElement<Stark252PrimeField>;
341→```
342→
343→### 4.1 `src/poseidon_hash.rs` — PoseidonHash
344→
345→Same XOF construction as Cairo. Base-Q extraction is trivial in Rust:
346→
347→```rust
348→const Q: u64 = 12289;
349→
350→pub struct PoseidonHash;
351→
352→impl PoseidonHash {
353→    pub fn hash_to_point(message: &[Felt], salt: &[Felt]) -> [u16; 512] {
354→        let mut state = [Felt::zero(); 3];
355→
356→        absorb(&mut state, message);
357→        absorb(&mut state, salt);
358→        state[2] += Felt::one();  // domain separation
359→
360→        let mut coeffs = [0u16; 512];
361→        let mut idx = 0;
362→        while idx < 512 {
363→            PoseidonCairoStark252::hades_permutation(&mut state);
364→            idx += extract_12_from_felt(&state[0], &mut coeffs, idx);
365→            if idx >= 512 { break; }
366→            idx += extract_12_from_felt(&state[1], &mut coeffs, idx);
367→        }
368→        coeffs
369→    }
370→}
371→
372→fn absorb(state: &mut [Felt; 3], input: &[Felt]) {
373→    let mut iter = input.iter();
374→    loop {
375→        match iter.next() {
376→            None => break,
377→            Some(first) => {
378→                state[0] += *first;
379→                match iter.next() {
380→                    Some(second) => state[1] += *second,
381→                    None => state[1] += Felt::one(),
382→                }
383→                PoseidonCairoStark252::hades_permutation(state);
384→            }
385→        }
386→    }
387→}
388→
389→fn extract_12_from_felt(value: &Felt, out: &mut [u16; 512], start: usize) -> usize {
390→    let bytes = value.to_bytes_be();
391→    let high = u128::from_be_bytes(bytes[0..16].try_into().unwrap());
392→    let low = u128::from_be_bytes(bytes[16..32].try_into().unwrap());
393→    let mut count = 0;
394→    count += extract_6_from_u128(low, out, start + count);
395→    count += extract_6_from_u128(high, out, start + count);
396→    count
397→}
398→
399→fn extract_6_from_u128(mut value: u128, out: &mut [u16; 512], start: usize) -> usize {
400→    for i in 0..6 {
401→        if start + i >= 512 { return i; }
402→        out[start + i] = (value % Q as u128) as u16;
403→        value /= Q as u128;
404→    }
405→    6
406→}
407→```
408→
409→### 4.2 `src/hints.rs` — Verification Hint Generation
410→
411→```rust
412→pub fn generate_mul_hint(s1: &[u16; 512], pk_h_ntt: &[u16; 512]) -> [u16; 512] {
413→    let s1_ntt = ntt(s1);
414→    let product_ntt: [i32; 512] = std::array::from_fn(|i| {
415→        ((s1_ntt[i] as i64 * pk_h_ntt[i] as i64) % Q as i64) as i32
416→    });
417→    let product = intt(&product_ntt);
418→    std::array::from_fn(|i| product[i].rem_euclid(Q as i32) as u16)
419→}
420→
421→pub fn generate_signature_with_hint(
422→    s1: &[u16; 512],
423→    salt: &[Felt],
424→    pk_h_ntt: &[u16; 512],
425→) -> FalconSignatureWithHint {
426→    let mul_hint = generate_mul_hint(s1, pk_h_ntt);
427→    FalconSignatureWithHint {
428→        signature: FalconSignature { s1: s1.to_vec(), salt: salt.to_vec() },
429→        hint: FalconVerificationHint { mul_hint: mul_hint.to_vec() },
430→    }
431→}
432→```
433→
434→### 4.3 `src/packing.rs` — Base-Q Public Key Packing
435→
436→```rust
437→const VALS_PER_U128: usize = 9;
438→const VALS_PER_FELT: usize = 18;
439→const PACKED_SLOTS: usize = 29;  // ceil(512 / 18)
440→
441→pub fn pack_public_key(h_ntt: &[u16; 512]) -> Vec<Felt> {
442→    h_ntt.chunks(VALS_PER_FELT).map(|chunk| {
443→        let (lo_vals, hi_vals) = chunk.split_at(chunk.len().min(VALS_PER_U128));
444→        let lo = horner_pack(lo_vals);
445→        let hi = horner_pack(hi_vals);
446→        // felt252 = lo + hi * 2^128
447→        Felt::from(lo) + Felt::from(hi) * TWO_POW_128
448→    }).collect()
449→}
450→
451→fn horner_pack(values: &[u16]) -> u128 {
452→    let mut acc: u128 = 0;
453→    for &v in values.iter().rev() {
454→        acc = acc * Q as u128 + v as u128;
455→    }
456→    acc
457→}
458→
459→pub fn unpack_public_key(packed: &[Felt]) -> Vec<u16> {
460→    // Reverse: split each felt252 into u128 halves, DivRem by Q chain
461→    ...
462→}
463→```
464→
465→### 4.4 `src/serialize.rs` — Output Formats
466→
467→**snforge JSON** (matches Cairo Serde deserialization with `pop_front` header skip):
468→
469→```rust
470→pub fn to_snforge_json(sig: &FalconSignatureWithHint) -> serde_json::Value {
471→    let mut payload: Vec<String> = Vec::new();
472→    // s1 array: [length, elem0, ...]
473→    payload.push(sig.signature.s1.len().to_string());
474→    for v in &sig.signature.s1 { payload.push(v.to_string()); }
475→    // salt array
476→    payload.push(sig.signature.salt.len().to_string());
477→    for s in &sig.signature.salt { payload.push(s.to_string()); }
478→    // mul_hint array
479→    payload.push(sig.hint.mul_hint.len().to_string());
480→    for v in &sig.hint.mul_hint { payload.push(v.to_string()); }
481→
482→    json!({ "signature_with_hint": payload })
483→}
484→```
485→
486→**Starknet calldata** (flat felt252 array for invoke transactions):
487→
488→```rust
489→pub fn to_calldata(sig: &FalconSignatureWithHint) -> Vec<Felt> {
490→    let mut calldata = Vec::new();
491→    serialize_u16_array(&sig.signature.s1, &mut calldata);
492→    serialize_felt_array(&sig.signature.salt, &mut calldata);
493→    serialize_u16_array(&sig.hint.mul_hint, &mut calldata);
494→    calldata
495→}
496→```
497→
498→### 4.5 `src/bin/falcon_tool.rs` — CLI
499→
500→```
501→falcon-tool generate-keypair                     → (sk.json, pk_packed.json)
502→falcon-tool sign --sk sk.json --message <felt>   → signature_with_hint.json
503→falcon-tool generate-test-data                   → all test vectors for Cairo snforge
504→```
505→
506→Test vectors generated:
507→- `hash_to_point_test.json` — (message, salt) → expected 512 coefficients
508→- `packing_test.json` — 512 Zq values → 29 packed felt252 → roundtrip
509→- `verify_test.json` — full FalconSignatureWithHint + public key + expected result
510→
511→### 4.6 HashToPoint Trait Update
512→
513→Generalize for both byte-based (Shake256) and field-based (Poseidon) inputs:
514→
515→```rust
516→pub trait HashToPoint {
517→    type Input;
518→    type Salt;
519→    fn hash_to_point(message: &[Self::Input], salt: &[Self::Salt]) -> [i16; 512];
520→}
521→
522→impl HashToPoint for Shake256Hash {
523→    type Input = u8;
524→    type Salt = u8;
525→    // existing impl
526→}
527→
528→impl HashToPoint for PoseidonHash {
