## Task 4: FalconAccountComponent

Write `packages/falcon_account/src/account.cairo`:

This is a `#[starknet::component]` that:
- Has 29 `felt252` storage slots (pk_0..pk_28) for the packed Falcon public key
- Implements ISRC6 (`__execute__`, `__validate__`, `is_valid_signature`)
- Implements IDeclarer (`__validate_declare__`)
- Implements IDeployable (`__validate_deploy__`)
- Has internal methods: `initializer`, `validate_transaction`, `_is_valid_signature`, `read_packed_pk`, `write_packed_pk`, `get_public_key`

Key details about the OZ interfaces we must implement:
```cairo
// From openzeppelin_interfaces::account::accounts
trait ISRC6<TState> {
    fn __execute__(self: @TState, calls: Array<Call>);
    fn __validate__(self: @TState, calls: Array<Call>) -> felt252;
    fn is_valid_signature(self: @TState, hash: felt252, signature: Array<felt252>) -> felt252;
}
trait IDeclarer<TState> {
    fn __validate_declare__(self: @TState, class_hash: felt252) -> felt252;
}
trait IDeployable<TState> {
    fn __validate_deploy__(self: @TState, class_hash: felt252, contract_address_salt: felt252, public_key: felt252) -> felt252;
}
// ISRC6_ID constant: 0x2ceccef7f994940b3962a6c67e0ba4fcd37df7d131417c604f91e03caecc1cd
```

Key imports available:
```cairo
use openzeppelin_interfaces::account::accounts as interface;  // contains ISRC6, IDeclarer, IDeployable, ISRC6_ID
use openzeppelin_introspection::src5::SRC5Component;
use openzeppelin_introspection::src5::SRC5Component::{InternalTrait as SRC5InternalTrait, SRC5Impl};
use openzeppelin_utils::execution::execute_single_call;
use starknet::account::Call;
use starknet::storage::{StoragePointerReadAccess, StoragePointerWriteAccess};
```

Validation flow:
```
__validate__ → validate_transaction() → get_tx_info().transaction_hash + .signature → _is_valid_signature(hash, signature)
_is_valid_signature → Serde::deserialize(signature) into PackedFalconSignatureWithHint → read_packed_pk() → verify_packed::<PoseidonHashToPoint>(@pk, sig, [hash])
```

`__execute__` must:
1. Assert caller is zero (protocol only)
2. Assert tx version is valid
3. Iterate calls and execute_single_call each

`_is_valid_signature` returns false (not panic) on deserialization failure or verification failure.

`is_valid_signature` returns `starknet::VALIDATED` on success, `0` on failure.

